// =============================================================================
// management-stewardship-course — "Management Is Stewardship"
// =============================================================================
// The CAPSTONE of the Real Estate department, and the second course built in it
// (DR-0500 opened the department with the footing). Darrell named these two ends
// himself: from why owned property is a principle through management as
// stewardship. Course one settled WHOSE the ground is; this one settles how a
// person runs ground that belongs to Another and to people who live on it.
//
// THE ARC, one argument in eight moves:
//   1. Faithful is the measurement (1 Corinthians 4:2; Luke 16:10)
//   2. Entrusted by ability, judged by action (Matthew 25:15, 21, 27)
//   3. Faithful in a very little, authority over ten cities (Luke 19:17)
//   4. The manager his owner stopped worrying about (Genesis 39:4, 6; 41:48)
//   5. The battlement: safety is blood, not a line item (Deuteronomy 22:8)
//   6. Their portion in due season (Luke 12:42, 48)
//   7. When management became extraction: restore, this day (Nehemiah 5:11, 15)
//   8. The account given with joy, and not with grief (Hebrews 13:17; Matthew 25:21)
//
// Metric -> entrustment -> scaling -> competence -> safety -> timeliness ->
// restitution -> the reckoning. Lesson 5 is the one place in the whole
// department where cost-benefit reasoning is ruled out by the text: the
// battlement is owed to an anonymous person who cannot inspect or negotiate,
// and the stated consequence is BLOOD upon the house. Lesson 7 is the hardest,
// because nothing in Nehemiah 5 was illegal and the remedy still carried a date.
//
// DELIBERATELY NO OVERLAP WITH COURSE ONE. That course used Leviticus 25,
// Deuteronomy 19, 1 Kings 21, Jeremiah 32, Ruth 4, Proverbs 24/27, Luke 14,
// Leviticus 19, Deuteronomy 24, James 5, Proverbs 13 and 1 Chronicles 28. This
// one stands on different passages throughout, because a capstone that
// re-preached the footing would teach nothing new while appearing to.
//
// AGE BANDS FROM THE FIRST COMMIT (DR-0497 / DR-0498). Every lesson carries
// levels.teen and levels.senior, authored rather than re-registered, so nothing
// here arrives in the course-band-coverage debt.
//
// VERIFICATION (DR-0076 / SCRIPTURE-REFERENCE-STANDARD). All 59 quoted spans
// were fetched VERBATIM from the repository's own KJV and are re-pinned by
// management-stewardship-course.test.js. The gate caught SIX elisions inside
// quotations in the first draft (DR-0459 forbids them); each was replaced with
// shorter genuinely-verbatim spans rather than an ellipsis, which is the only
// remedy that rule allows. Our prose says Yahweh; quotations keep "the LORD"
// exactly as the KJV has it (DR-0210's bright line).
//
// TEACHING, NOT LEGAL OR FINANCIAL ADVICE, carried on the meta so every surface
// renders the limit with the course.
// =============================================================================

