    levels: {
      teen: 'A man goes away and leaves money with his workers to run. When he comes back, one of them did well. Watch what he gets. Not a bonus. Not a thank-you gift. "Well, thou good servant: because thou hast been faithful in a very little, have thou authority over ten cities" (Luke 19:17). Ten cities. Because of A VERY LITTLE. Put those two side by side, because that is the lesson. The test was tiny. The promotion was enormous. This is how it actually works, and most people get it backwards. They think: give me something big and then you will see what I can do. Yahweh works the other way. Show me the small thing done right, and I will widen the ground under you. And notice what the reward IS. It is not a vacation. It is ten cities to look after. More weight, not less. If that sounds hard, it is — but it is also the only honest promotion there is. So stop waiting to be handed something worth your effort. Whatever is in your hand right now is the interview. Here is a test you can actually run. Look at the smallest thing you are responsible for. Now imagine somebody deciding whether to hand you ten times more, and the only thing they are allowed to look at is that small thing. What would they decide? That is not unfair. That is just how trust gets built, and it is the same way Yahweh does it. Fix the small thing and the decision changes by itself, without you making a single speech. And do not skip the other half. Ten cities is not a vacation. It is ten cities to look after. If you want more, want the weight too, because that is what more actually is.',
      senior: 'Teach this as the scaling doctrine of the whole department, and teach it against the way the trade talks about growth. The commendation is exact: "Well, thou good servant: because thou hast been faithful in a very little, have thou authority over ten cities" (Luke 19:17). Set the two quantities beside each other — a VERY LITTLE on one side, TEN CITIES on the other. The disproportion is the doctrine. Three things follow, and each corrects a common error. First, scope is granted on EVIDENCE, not on appetite. The servant did not petition for cities; he was observed. A manager building a case for a larger portfolio out of ambition rather than a record is asking to be trusted where he has not been tested. Second, the reward of good management is more management. Ten cities is weight, not leisure — which means the honest way to describe a promotion in this trade is an increase in what can go wrong under your name. Anyone who wants scale without that is wanting the wrong object. Third, and pastorally: the small charge is not a waiting room. It is the examination, running now, and it is the only examination there is. Luke 16:10 has already said the same thing from the other side. The application is plain enough to be uncomfortable. If a manager wants more doors, the case is not a pitch — it is the record on the doors he has: the vacancy days, the response times, the deposits accounted to the dollar, the repairs logged the day they happened. An owner who cannot see that record has nothing to promote on, and a manager who cannot produce it has already answered the question.',
    },
    lesson: 'The parable of the pounds pays a good manager in a currency worth noticing: "Well, thou good servant: because thou hast been faithful in a very little, have thou authority over ten cities" (Luke 19:17). Hold the two quantities side by side, because the disproportion IS the teaching — a very little on one side of the sentence, ten cities on the other. THREE THINGS FOLLOW, and each one corrects a mistake this trade makes constantly. FIRST, SCOPE IS GRANTED ON EVIDENCE, NOT ON APPETITE. The servant did not petition for cities; he was observed. A manager who builds a case for a larger portfolio out of ambition rather than out of a record is asking to be trusted where he has not yet been tested, and the honest answer to him is not cruelty, it is arithmetic: there is nothing to judge him on. The record is the application. SECOND, THE REWARD FOR GOOD MANAGEMENT IS MORE MANAGEMENT. Ten cities is not a holiday; it is ten cities of weight. So the honest description of a promotion in this work is an increase in what can go wrong under your name, and an increase in the number of people whose homes depend on your attention. Anyone who wants scale without that wants the wrong object, and will resent the thing they asked for within a year. THIRD, AND SAY THIS ONE GENTLY, because most people in the room need it: the small charge is not a waiting room. It is the examination, and it is running right now, and it is the only examination there is. One rental, one building, one street of doors — that is the very little out of which ten cities are given. Luke 16:10 said the same thing from the other direction: he that is faithful in that which is least is faithful also in much. NOW MAKE IT OPERATIONAL, because the principle is useless as a sentiment. If a manager wants more doors, the case is not a pitch and never was. It is the record on the doors he already has: days to fill a vacancy, hours to answer a call, deposits accounted to the dollar, repairs logged on the day they happened, rent collected without a single tenant humiliated. An owner who cannot see that record has nothing to promote on. A manager who cannot produce it has already answered the question he came to ask. And the manager who CAN produce it rarely has to pitch at all — which is what the verse has been saying the whole time.',
